# OCS VR training walkthrough (sessions, scores, progress).
# Select the REST Client environment, then send each numbered request top to bottom,
# checking the expected status in its heading. REST Client keeps the login cookie.
# Creates real rows in the selected environment: training sessions for the account you sign in as.
# The VR app sends the same requests; scripts/verify_training.py checks them automatically.
@module = build_computer.identify_components

### 1. Authenticate as any active account (expect 200)
# @name login
# @prompt uid Enter your user ID
# @prompt password Enter your password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "uid": "{{uid}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 2. Who am I? The uid here is the learner_id of every session below (expect 200)
# @name me
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/id
Accept: application/json

### 3. Start a session: a mission begins (expect 201 with a session_id, status "started")
# @name start
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sessions/start
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "module": "{{module}}",
  "device": "quest3"
}

### 4. Complete it: the mission ended (expect 200, status "completed")
# The server sets the learner and the times itself; a learner_id or timestamp in the body is not saved.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sessions/complete
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "session_id": "{{start.response.body.$.session_id}}",
  "module": "{{module}}",
  "status": "completed",
  "attempts": 2,
  "duration_s": 184,
  "score": 85,
  "device": "quest3"
}

### 5. Complete it again, as a retry would (expect 200 with the result from step 4, unchanged)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sessions/complete
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "session_id": "{{start.response.body.$.session_id}}",
  "attempts": 1,
  "duration_s": 10,
  "score": 100
}

### 6. Complete a mission in one request, with no start (expect 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sessions/complete
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "module": "build_network.connect_two_computers",
  "attempts": 1,
  "duration_s": 60,
  "score": 70,
  "device": "desktop"
}

### 7. A score out of range (expect 400 naming the field)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sessions/complete
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "module": "{{module}}",
  "attempts": 1,
  "duration_s": 60,
  "score": 101
}

### 8. A score for somebody else (expect 403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sessions/complete
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "learner_id": "somebody-else",
  "module": "{{module}}",
  "attempts": 1,
  "duration_s": 60,
  "score": 100
}

### 9. A session_id that does not exist (expect 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sessions/complete
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "session_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000",
  "attempts": 1,
  "duration_s": 60,
  "score": 100
}

### 10. My progress: totals, one line per module, recent sessions (expect 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/learners/{{me.response.body.$.uid}}/progress
Accept: application/json

### 11. Somebody else's progress (expect 200 as a Teacher or Admin, 403 as anyone else)
# @prompt learner Enter another learner's user ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/learners/{{learner}}/progress
Accept: application/json
